Bundled software
----------------
The jar, the runtime images and the container image include these libraries, each
under its own license (the license texts are in licenses/ in the runtime images
and in /opt/accessconverter/licenses/ in the container image):

- Jackcess (https://github.com/spannm/jackcess), Apache License 2.0
- Jackcess Encrypt (https://github.com/jahlborn/jackcessencrypt),
  Apache License 2.0
- Bouncy Castle (bcprov-jdk18on) (https://www.bouncycastle.org), MIT License,
  Copyright (c) 2000-2026 The Legion of the Bouncy Castle Inc.
- SQLite JDBC (https://github.com/xerial/sqlite-jdbc), Apache License
  2.0; it contains SQLite (https://sqlite.org), which is in the public domain
- Jackson core (https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson-core), Apache License 2.0
- picocli (https://picocli.info), Apache License 2.0

The runtime images also contain a Java runtime built from OpenJDK (Eclipse
Temurin), licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2, with the
Classpath Exception; its notices are in runtime/legal/. The container image is
based on gcr.io/distroless/java21-debian12, which carries its own notices.

Test data
---------
The test suite downloads Access databases from these projects, pinned by commit
and checksum in src/test/resources/fixtures/corpus.tsv:

- Jackcess (https://github.com/spannm/jackcess, src/test/resources/data),
  licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
- Jackcess Encrypt (https://github.com/jahlborn/jackcessencrypt, src/test/data),
  licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
- mdb-reader (https://github.com/andipaetzold/mdb-reader, test/), licensed under
  the MIT License

They are fetched at build time into target/fixtures/ and are not distributed with
AccessConverter.
